            Node("canonicalIndex", F0(), "The displayed defining equation retains the data fields; proof fields are omitted by proof irrelevance.", DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source)),
            Node("claim", F1(), "Christiansen, Section 1.1, p. 4, Conjecture 3, verbatim: “Let Φ ∈ 𝔥 ∧ 𝔥 be normalized with canonical form Φ = ∑_{k=1}^{∞} λ_k u_k ∧ v_k. Then there exists a constant C > 0, independent of Φ, such that for every N ∈ 2ℕ with N λ_max² ≤ 1 sup_{Ψ ∈ ⋀ᴺ𝔥, ‖Ψ‖=1} ⟨Φ, γ₂^Ψ Φ⟩ ≤ N(1 − (N−2)/2 ∑_{k=1}^{∞} λ_k⁴ + C(N λ_max²)²).”. The displayed claim fixes C = 5/8. H is an arbitrary separable complex Hilbert space; Φ has the supplied normalized canonical form, v(i,0) and v(i,1) are mutually orthonormal, and m parametrizes N = 2m + 2. The physical tensor permutation action defines fermionic antisymmetry. sourceRayleigh uses the literal creation/annihilation-kernel RDM, with trace N(N−1). lambdaMax is the attained maximum. The source supremum is encoded by quantifying every normalized ψ.", DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source)),
            Node("lambdaMax", F2(), "The displayed defining equation retains the data fields; proof fields are omitted by proof irrelevance.", DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source)),
            Node("physicalParticle", F3(), "The displayed defining equation retains the data fields; proof fields are omitted by proof irrelevance.", DescribeRole.Definition, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source)),
            Node("result", F4(), "The claim holds with C = 5/8. The weighted occupation-row estimate retains the fourth moment, spectator modes, weight one at zero coefficient, and the original unrenormalized cutoffs.", DescribeRole.Theorem, AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(Source)))));
